Unreleased
---
Feature
- The dependency graph is queryable: dependenciesOf(), dependentsOf() and
  missingDependenciesOf(). The manager has always resolved the graph -
  topologically, rejecting cycles and version mismatches with a diagnosable
  message - but only as a step of loadPlugins(), so the answer existed only
  afterwards and only as a load order. A window that lets someone switch a
  plugin off has to say beforehand who goes down with it, and these answer from
  the metadata, so they work before anything is loaded.
  tst_QxPlugin::dependencyGraph

0.2.1
---
Bugfix
- QX_PLUGIN_DEPRECATED_SINCE(major, minor) never answered true for a deprecation
  that had already happened: QX_PLUGIN_DISABLE_DEPRECATED_BEFORE defaulted to
  QX_PLUGIN_VERSION, so the deprecation point was compared against the version
  being built - (0,2,0) > (0,2,0) is false - and the answer flipped back to false
  on every minor bump. The default is now a fixed floor, so an API stays declared
  for as long as it is inside its removal buffer (K26), and raising the cutoff is
  what compiles it out. tst_qxdeprecated covers all seven libraries
